    "https://job-portal.lmu.de/jobposting/d8cb0357b3fd8a578b046958bcc8ca1d25fe0a770": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher (m/f/x)",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher (m/f/x) | Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München | 4566 Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München is a leading research university in Europe. Since its founding in 1472 it has been committed to the highest international standards of excellence in research and teaching. Institution Faculty of Philosophy, Philosophy of Science and the Study of Religion - Chair of Metaphysics (Prof. Alyssa Ney) Remuneration group TV-L E13 Full-time / Part-time Full-time (100%) Start date 2027-01-15; limited to three years About us: The Chair of Metaphysics (Prof. Dr. Alyssa Ney) investigates metaphysical topics from an analytical perspective, aiming for an approach that is scientifically based, historically informed, and socially engaged. We are looking for you: Postdoctoral Researcher (m/f/x) in Munich Your tasks and responsibilities: The candidate will be expected to maintain an active research program in metaphysics and the philosophy of physics, including on metaphysical questions related to QBism and/or quantum information theory. They will also be expected to participate in the weekly group activities of the ERC project. The position will include some administrative tasks, such as the organization of workshops. Your qualifications: Candidates are required to have a doctorate in philosophy, with an AOS in Philosophy of Physics and Metaphysics. Additional background training in physics is welcome. This is a research-only position, and all work will be conducted in English. Benefits: The Chair of Metaphysics in the Faculty of Philosophy at LMU Munich invites applications for two postdoc positions in a European Research Council supported project on the metaphysics of quantum physics. These are fixed term (non-tenure track) postdoctoral positions that run for three years. The starting date is January 15, 2027. Remuneration is based on the TV-L E13 pay scale (100%). The Chair of Metaphysics is a vibrant center of research at LMU Munich, which hosts regular workshops, a colloquium series, and other events through the academic year. Prospective applicants can learn more about the Chair by visiting here . Applications from women and members of underrepresented groups are expressly welcome. Also possible in a part-time capacity. People with disabilities who are equally as qualified as other applicants will receive preferential treatment. Contact: Applications should be written entirely in English and include the following: letter of interest CV with certificates writing sample research plan (maximum three pages) the names and e-mail addresses of three professors who can send letters of recommendation, if requested. These materials should be compiled into a single PDF and sent by October 15, 2026 at the latest to: office.ney@lrz.uni-muenchen.de . The e-mail subject line should include \"ERC postdoc application\" and the applicant's name. Where knowledge is everything. LMU researchers work at the highest level on the great questions affecting people, society, culture, the environment and technology — supported by experts in administration, IT and tech. Become part of LMU Munich! In the course of your application for an open position at Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität (LMU) München, you will be required to submit personal information. Please be sure to refer to our LMU Privacy Policy . By submitting your application, you confirm that you have read and understood our data protection guidelines and privacy policy and that you agree to your data being processed in accordance with the selection process. Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 80539 München www.lmu.de Imprint Accessibility Back to the LMU Job Portal"
